46	 * shopper's browser language disagrees with the storefront they're currently on, and if so,
47	 * which of the four EU languages to offer switching to.
48	 *
49	 * Both sides of the comparison are reduced to their primary subtag before comparing — browsers
50	 * report full tags (`fr-FR`, `it-CH`), and one of our own site locales is itself a full tag
51	 * (`en-GB`) rather than a bare code. Comparing full strings would make a French shopper
52	 * reporting `fr-FR` never match anything, and would make `en-GB` (our own English site's
53	 * locale) never match a browser reporting plain `en`.
54	 *
55	 * Only `browserLanguages[0]` (the browser's single most-preferred language) is evaluated, not
56	 * the full preference list — every branch this predicate needs to support describes "the
57	 * browser's language" as one signal, and scanning further down an unmatched preference list for
58	 * a supported one is a behaviour nothing has specified.
59	 *
